From: PulsarOS Build System
Date: 2025-06-02
Subject: [PATCH] Fix CONF_ANDROID_MAJOR_VER macro redefinition in libcedarx

The libcedarx library (Allwinner video decoder) defines CONF_ANDROID_MAJOR_VER
multiple times in its Android.bp with conflicting values (12 and 10). This causes
-Werror,-Wmacro-redefined compilation errors.

Remove the redundant CONF_ANDROID_MAJOR_VER=10 definition, keeping only =12
which matches the Android 12 build target.

--- a/frameworks/av/media/libcedarx/libcore/base/Android.bp
+++ b/frameworks/av/media/libcedarx/libcore/base/Android.bp
@@ -38,7 +38,6 @@ cc_defaults {
         "-DCONF_KITKAT_AND_NEWER",
         "-DCONF_JB42_AND_NEWER",
         "-DCONF_ANDROID_MAJOR_VER=12",
-        "-DCONF_ANDROID_MAJOR_VER=10",
         "-DCONF_ANDROID_SUB_VER=1",
         "-DCONF_KERNEL_VERSION_4_9",
         "-DCONF_GPU_MALI",
